# LeakSanitizer suppressions for Threads.mtapps, on top of
# src/tests/lsan.supp (CMake joins the two files for this test only).
#
# Policy, as for tsan.supp: only leaks that libX11 or libXt make and
# lose themselves, each with the reason it is not a Motif bug.  A leak
# of memory that Motif holds or frees is a Motif bug: fix it.

# libX11: now and then, 8 bytes that _XimOpenIM allocates (the input
# method name, from _XimMakeImName) are lost while the rest of the XIM
# is freed; Motif never sees that string.  Only seen with several
# threads opening input methods at once (Ubuntu clang debug-asan, PR
# #19).  It is scoped to this test because the pattern also matches the
# XIM record itself, which would leak if Motif failed to XCloseIM: the
# single-threaded suites keep catching that.
leak:_XimOpenIM
